{
  "name": "hp-solicited",
  "why": "F264: a hit, then the poll's probe answered by the gun (a solicited `$HP` with the same pools: no damage), then the gun goes dead behind the node's back and the next poll answer `$HP,0` books a desync death.",
  "source": "app/test/engine.test.mjs F264 poll tests; app/src/engine.js `_onHp` `solicited`",
  "runners": ["engine","stage"],
  "setup": {
    "delay": "timers",
    "fields": ["moment"]
  },
  "steps": [
    {"advance_ms":10},
    {"advance_ms":3000},
    {"check":"live","preamble":true},
    {"frames":["$HIR,4,0,19,2,9,0,3,*","$HP,45,61,0,*"]},
    {"check":"hit"},
    {"advance_ms":21000},
    {"check":"poll_answered"},
    {"gun":{"hp":0,"armor":0}},
    {"advance_ms":21000},
    {"check":"poll_finds_zero"}
  ],
  "stage_ignores": [
    {"what":"checkpoint:poll_finds_zero:writes","why":"DIVERGENCE: the engine's F272 liveness probe (`_sendGunProbe`, KNOWN_UNMIRRORED) finds the dead gun and books the desync death with its follow-up writes; the stage asks the gun less often (its own poll), so its pools and writes differ at this checkpoint."},
    {"what":"state.armor","at":"poll_finds_zero","why":"DIVERGENCE: the engine's F272 liveness probe (`_sendGunProbe`, KNOWN_UNMIRRORED) finds the dead gun and books the desync death with its follow-up writes; the stage asks the gun less often (its own poll), so its pools and writes differ at this checkpoint."},
    {"what":"state.hp","at":"poll_finds_zero","why":"DIVERGENCE: the engine's F272 liveness probe (`_sendGunProbe`, KNOWN_UNMIRRORED) finds the dead gun and books the desync death with its follow-up writes; the stage asks the gun less often (its own poll), so its pools and writes differ at this checkpoint."},
    {"what":"state.alive","at":"poll_finds_zero","why":"DIVERGENCE: the engine's F272 liveness probe (`_sendGunProbe`, KNOWN_UNMIRRORED) finds the dead gun and books the desync death; the stage asks the gun less often (its own poll), so it books it at another checkpoint."},
    {"what":"write:$LIFE,0,0,0,*","why":"Deliberate, not a divergence: the F272 gun liveness probe (engine.js `_sendGunProbe`) is on test_stage_mirror.py's KNOWN_UNMIRRORED list, so the stage has only the divergence poll and asks the gun with `$LIFE,0,0,0,*` less often."},
    {"what":"write:$GLED","why":"Harness timing: the stage's gun-body readout animation runs on its injected `sleep`, which is instant in this runner, while the engine's runs on its tick clock, so the same frames land at different checkpoints."},
    {"what":"state.moment","why":"The stage has no HUD moment slot to expose as state (its `_moment` is an internal gate); the HUD reads the engine's."},
    {"what":"state.deaths","why":"The stage keeps no death count (MC and the HUD read the engine's); `alive` is compared instead."},
    {"what":"state.phase","why":"The stage has no MC link, so it has no match phase; it is armed and spawned by its own buttons."}
  ],
